Package: ${PACKAGE_NAME}
Version: $VERSION
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Installed-Size: $INSTALLED_SIZE
Depends: bash (>= 5), parted, e2fsprogs, rsync, whiptail, dosfstools, fdisk, curl
Recommends: bash-completion
Suggests: pv, jq, lsof, btrfs-progs, f2fs-tools, mailutils, default-mta | msmtp-mta | mail-transport-agent
Maintainer: framp <framp@linux-tips-and-tricks.de>
Homepage: https://raspibackup.linux-tips-and-tricks.de
Description: Backup and restore tool for Raspberry Pi systems
 raspiBackup creates full backups (images) of a running Raspberry Pi
 with dd, tar or rsync, including incremental rsync backups with hardlinks.
 Backups can be stored on a USB disk, NAS (NFS, SMB/CIFS) or any mounted
 device, and are restored to an SD card, USB disk, SSD or NVMe with
 raspiBackup itself. Supports Raspberry Pi OS (Raspbian) and Ubuntu.
 .
 Old backup versions are deleted automatically: either a fixed number
 of backups is kept, or smart recycle applies a more sophisticated
 strategy. Backups are scheduled with a systemd timer, email and other
 notifications report the result. raspiBackupConfig configures all of
 it in a menu. Sample extensions run your own code before and after a
 backup at different extension points.
